{
  "$comment": "Single source of truth for design §6.1/§6.2 module boundaries. Consumed by packages/config/eslint/node.mjs (static enforcement) and by the boundary test in apps/api (table ownership). Every §7.2 table appears in exactly one module's `owns` list, or in `shared`. A module directory missing from `modules[]` is invisible to moduleOfPath, so its edges are allowed by default: `m25-workflow-egress` is in that state (see ADR-BE-18, deferred work). Registering a module is a deliberate edit, never a silent default.",
  "root": "apps/api/src/modules",
  "crossCutting": ["M15", "M17"],
  "shared": {
    "$comment": "Tables with more than one legitimate writer. Only the named repository may write them; the boundary test still checks that no module defines its own DDL-owning repository for these.",
    "outbox": "M17",
    "settings": "M09"
  },
  "runtime": [
    {
      "$comment": "Directories under apps/api/src that are platform machinery rather than a product domain, yet still name tables. They were a hard-coded map inside the boundary test; declaring them here means a new directory cannot avoid the rule by being new, and the test stops special-casing TypeScript. `audit` and `secrets` are absent because they are now `modules/m17-audit` and `modules/m15-secrets`, where their contracts already were.",
      "dir": "bootstrap",
      "owns": [],
      "reads": []
    },
    { "dir": "common", "owns": [], "reads": [] },
    { "dir": "config", "owns": [], "reads": [] },
